     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Mike,</div><div><br></div><div>Are the amphibreed and amphistage arguments functional in ectotherm()? If so, might you be able to provide a worked code example of using them (in whatever fashion is convenient to you)? I&#39;ve been doing some testing and haven&#39;t yet established how these arguments are best employed – for instance, if amphibreed = 1 (entailing exotrophic aquatic), should the initial stage = 0 (embryo) or 3 (an adult beyond first reproduction). And presumably these arguments are only operational when the water body model is running (container = 1). I haven&#39;t found documentation or published work online but apologies if I&#39;ve missed something.</div><div><br></div><div>Best and thanks,</div><div>Dave</div><div><br></div><span class=\"gmail_signature_prefix\">-- </span><br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size:small\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"4\" color=\"#666666\" face=\"times new roman, serif\">David Klinges, PhD</font></div><div><img width=\"200\" height=\"75\" src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/mail-sig/AIorK4xY-XSJuf3_zCBzgEXqeW1GOzgHTiSkQRWnzpxOYB5iBxRI1fnIcrYjfvIVKZyFNUZdzsmZ8qLFeQZM\"><br></div><div><a href=\"https://natureinparadise.github.io/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://natureinparadise.github.io/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793239639978000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3CDKVy6WkJyC7nkSdvj_0F\"><i>https://natureinparadise.github.io/</i></a></div></div><div><i><a href=\"https://48b294cf.streaklinks.com/CX9zlgwoqJ6A1fxdcANQ2PQ